{"timestamp": "2026-08-09T19:37:31.960317+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "logger": "openai._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'User-Agent': 'pydantic-ai/1.107.1'}, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-3a1d45e5-0d86-4b17-a4fa-4682fed2f022', 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': 'You prepare the educational structure of one approved lesson.\\n\\nThe path owns the objective. The skeleton owns section count, order, and purpose.\\nA later planner will choose page blocks. You must not choose components, page\\nobjects, layouts, or question text.\\n\\n## FIXED INPUT\\n\\n- objective and objective_hash\\n- concept_id\\n- primary_knowledge_type\\n- lesson_mode\\n- ordered skeleton slots\\n- scope_contract\\n- prior_established\\n- explicit prerequisites\\n- lesson_actuals\\n- carried anchor, when present\\n- resource identity and purpose\\n\\n## YOUR DECISIONS\\n\\n1. Draft zero to three real misconceptions. Each must support a confident wrong\\n   answer. A missing term is a knowledge gap, not a misconception.\\n2. Reuse the carried anchor when it fits. Otherwise choose one concrete anchor\\n   and state why it is new.\\n3. Give each fixed section a concise title and transition note.\\n4. Preserve section IDs and roles exactly as supplied.\\n5. Attach the canonical concept card ID where required.\\n\\n## PROHIBITIONS\\n\\n- Never change the objective or concept ID.\\n- Never add, remove, reorder, or rename a skeleton slot.\\n- Never choose a component, page object, pedagogical block intent, placement,\\n  or visual form.\\n- Never write question text.\\n- Never reteach prior_established in the structural rationale.\\n- Never introduce must_not_introduce content.\\n- Never manufacture a misconception to fill a count.\\n- Never choose page blocks, intents, objects, or briefs. A later planner\\n  owns the teaching design.\\n\\nIf the objective cannot honestly fit the skeleton, emit deviation_request.\\nIf the objective itself is wrong, emit objective_concern. Do not repair either.\\n\\n## OUTPUT\\n\\nJSON only, matching the supplied output schema.\\n\\nThe output contains:\\n\\n- anchor\\n- one concept card\\n- sections with id, title, role, card_id, visual_required, transition_note\\n- deviation_request or null\\n- objective_concern or null\\n\\nIt contains no components and no blocks.\\n\\n## SELF-CHECK\\n\\n1. Is the objective verbatim?\\n2. Do section IDs and order exactly match the fixed slots?\\n3. Does every misconception pass the confident-wrong-answer test?\\n4. Did I choose any page form or teaching block? Remove it.\\n5. Did I contradict prior_established, terminology, or exclusions?\\n'}, {'role': 'system', 'content': 'Return only valid JSON matching this schema.\\nDo not call tools.\\n{\"$defs\": {\"PathAnchor\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"source\": {\"enum\": [\"carried\", \"new\"], \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"description\", \"source\"], \"title\": \"PathAnchor\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"PathDeviationRequest\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"operation\": {\"enum\": [\"insert\", \"remove\", \"replace\", \"reorder\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, \"target_slot\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"replacement_slot\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}]}, \"reason\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"operation\", \"target_slot\", \"replacement_slot\", \"reason\"], \"title\": \"PathDeviationRequest\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"PathStructuralCard\": {\"properties\": {\"id\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"description\": \"Echo concept_id verbatim. The path layer owns this value.\"}, \"title\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"objective\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"description\": \"Echo the supplied objective verbatim. Never rewrite it.\"}, \"prereqs\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"misconceptions\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/PathStructuralMisconception\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"no_known_misconceptions\": {\"default\": false, \"type\": \"boolean\"}, \"opens_by\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"title\": \"PathStructuralCard\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"PathStructuralComponentSlot\": {\"description\": \"Legacy component-selector shape. Ignored entirely on the native page path.\", \"properties\": {\"slug\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"purpose\": {\"default\": \"\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"reason\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"required\": [\"slug\"], \"title\": \"PathStructuralComponentSlot\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"PathStructuralMisconception\": {\"properties\": {\"id\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"description\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"description\": \"The wrong belief, stated the way a learner would state it.\"}, \"statement\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"source\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"title\": \"PathStructuralMisconception\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"PathStructuralSection\": {\"properties\": {\"id\": {\"description\": \"Must equal slots[i].slot_id verbatim, in the supplied order. The field is named \\'id\\' \\\\u2014 do not emit a key called \\'slot_id\\'.\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"role\": {\"description\": \"Must ALSO equal slots[i].slot_id verbatim \\\\u2014 not slots[i].role.\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": {\"description\": \"Concise section title. Aim for ~80 chars (advisory).\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"card_id\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"description\": \"concept_id for teaching sections; null for plain sections.\"}, \"visual_required\": {\"default\": false, \"type\": \"boolean\"}, \"transition_note\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"description\": \"Why this section follows the previous one. Null for the first section only. Aim for ~120 chars (advisory).\"}, \"components\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/PathStructuralComponentSlot\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"role\", \"title\"], \"title\": \"PathStructuralSection\", \"type\": \"object\"}}, \"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"anchor\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/PathAnchor\"}, \"cards\": {\"description\": \"Exactly one concept card, unless emitting objective_concern.\", \"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/PathStructuralCard\"}, \"maxItems\": 1, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"sections\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/PathStructuralSection\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"deviation_request\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/PathDeviationRequest\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"objective_concern\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"required\": [\"anchor\"], \"title\": \"PathStructuralPlan\", \"type\": \"object\"}'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '{\\n  \"component_selections\": {},\\n  \"concept_id\": \"fce6a245-18bb-4cdf-9fc9-0d81a6f2ebb0\",\\n  \"exclusions\": [],\\n  \"external_prerequisites\": [],\\n  \"group_ids\": [],\\n  \"groups\": [],\\n  \"lesson_actuals\": [],\\n  \"must_establish\": [\\n    \"Plants are called producers because they produce their own food.\",\\n    \"Making food is necessary for energy and growth, just like eating is for animals.\"\\n  ],\\n  \"native_whole_lesson\": true,\\n  \"objective\": \"Identify that plants are producers because they make their own food, unlike animals that eat other living things.\",\\n  \"objective_hash\": \"ea0293035edd55b66b31f8dbce87f884823264ebf3d6c4e5f1b577abf37e1f90\",\\n  \"prerequisites\": [],\\n  \"primary_knowledge_type\": \"conceptual\",\\n  \"prior_established\": [\\n    \"plants are living things that need certain things to grow and stay healthy\",\\n    \"plants have roots, stems, and leaves that each do a job\",\\n    \"animals get food by eating other living things, but plants do something different\"\\n  ],\\n  \"scope_contract\": {\\n    \"assumed_prerequisites\": [],\\n    \"may_include\": [],\\n    \"must_establish\": [\\n      \"Explain why light is essential for plants to make food.\",\\n      \"Understand that plants are producers that make their own food through photosynthesis.\",\\n      \"Identify the inputs (carbon dioxide, water, light) and outputs (sugar, oxygen) of photosynthesis and that light provides the energy.\"\\n    ],\\n    \"must_not_introduce\": [\\n      \"Detailed chemical equations (e.g., 6CO\\\\u2082 + 6H\\\\u2082O \\\\u2192 C\\\\u2086H\\\\u2081\\\\u2082O\\\\u2086 + 6O\\\\u2082)\",\\n      \"Cellular respiration\",\\n      \"Chloroplast structure at the molecular level\",\\n      \"Light-dependent and light-independent reactions\",\\n      \"Quantitative limiting factors\"\\n    ],\\n    \"notation\": null,\\n    \"terminology\": [\\n      \"producer\",\\n      \"photosynthesis\",\\n      \"chlorophyll\",\\n      \"carbon dioxide\",\\n      \"oxygen\",\\n      \"sugar\"\\n    ]\\n  },\\n  \"secondary_demand\": null,\\n  \"slots\": [\\n    {\\n      \"allowed_components\": [\\n        \"hook-hero\",\\n        \"interview-anchor\",\\n        \"insight-strip\",\\n        \"timeline-block\"\\n      ],\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Give the learner a reason to care and a concrete situation to hold.\",\\n      \"role\": \"orient\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"orient\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"allowed_components\": [\\n        \"explanation-block\",\\n        \"definition-card\",\\n        \"definition-family\",\\n        \"key-fact\",\\n        \"diagram-block\",\\n        \"insight-strip\",\\n        \"callout-block\"\\n      ],\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Build the idea itself. State it, ground it, make it usable.\",\\n      \"role\": \"explain\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"explain\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"allowed_components\": [\\n        \"comparison-grid\",\\n        \"diagram-compare\",\\n        \"definition-family\",\\n        \"key-fact\"\\n      ],\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Put a case and a near-miss side by side. The learner must see the boundary of the idea, not just the idea.\\\\n\",\\n      \"role\": \"contrast\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"contrast\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"allowed_components\": [\\n        \"quiz-check\"\\n      ],\\n      \"locked\": true,\\n      \"purpose\": \"The shared diagnostic. Identical across every variant. Written from the card only, never from the prose above it.\\\\n\",\\n      \"role\": \"check\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"check\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \"title\": \"Plants as Producers\",\\n  \"variant_previews\": [\\n    {\\n      \"blocking_issues\": [],\\n      \"group_profile\": \"core\",\\n      \"slots\": [\\n        {\\n          \"allowed_components\": [\\n            \"hook-hero\",\\n            \"interview-anchor\",\\n            \"insight-strip\",\\n            \"timeline-block\"\\n          ],\\n          \"locked\": false,\\n          \"purpose\": \"Give the learner a reason to care and a concrete situation to hold.\",\\n          \"role\": \"orient\",\\n          \"slot_id\": \"orient\",\\n          \"visual_required\": false\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"allowed_components\": [\\n            \"explanation-block\",\\n            \"definition-card\",\\n            \"definition-family\",\\n            \"key-fact\",\\n            \"diagram-block\",\\n            \"insight-strip\",\\n            \"callout-block\"\\n          ],\\n          \"locked\": false,\\n          \"purpose\": \"Build the idea itself. State it, ground it, make it usable.\",\\n          \"role\": \"explain\",\\n          \"slot_id\": \"explain\",\\n          \"visual_required\": false\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"allowed_components\": [\\n            \"comparison-grid\",\\n            \"diagram-compare\",\\n            \"definition-family\",\\n            \"key-fact\"\\n          ],\\n          \"locked\": false,\\n          \"purpose\": \"Put a case and a near-miss side by side. The learner must see the boundary of the idea, not just the idea.\\\\n\",\\n          \"role\": \"contrast\",\\n          \"slot_id\": \"contrast\",\\n          \"visual_required\": false\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"allowed_components\": [\\n            \"quiz-check\"\\n          ],\\n          \"locked\": true,\\n          \"purpose\": \"The shared diagnostic. Identical across every variant. Written from the card only, never from the prose above it.\\\\n\",\\n          \"role\": \"check\",\\n          \"slot_id\": \"check\",\\n          \"visual_required\": false\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \"structural_diff\": [\\n        {\\n          \"explanation\": \"No unaddressed approved misconception needs this confrontation slot.\",\\n          \"operation\": \"remove\",\\n          \"replacement_slot\": null,\\n          \"slot_id\": \"confront\",\\n          \"toggle_id\": \"misconception.confront_per_belief\"\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \"support_level\": \"medium\",\\n      \"toggles_applied\": [\\n        \"misconception.confront_per_belief\"\\n      ],\\n      \"warnings\": []\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}'}], 'model': 'deepseek-v4-pro', 'max_completion_tokens': 120000, 'stream': False}}"}
